{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who is like You among the elim.</b> He gives praise to El, blessed be He, for His third battle, against the multitude of Egyptian chariots, and says: Who is like You among the mighty, who can alter the nature of beings that are incorruptible by their nature." "<b>Glorified in holiness.</b> Now, the holy in the absolute sense is that which is incorruptible entirely, as the Sages said, blessed be their memory (Sanhedrin 92a): the dead whom the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to revive do not return to dust, as it says (Isaiah 4:3): ״הַנִּשְׁאָר בִּירוּשָׁלַיִם קָדוֹשׁ יֵאָמֵר לוֹ״ — just as the holy endures forever, etc. He says that none is known as exalted like El, blessed be He, king over all holy and eternal elim; and therefore to Him alone is it fitting to alter the nature of any being that is incorruptible, for the eternity of any eternal thing is from none other than Him, blessed be He." "<b>Awesome in praises.</b> And whoever knows the greatness of His praises will fear Him for His own sake — not out of fear of punishment that may come from Him." "<b>Doer of wonder.</b> Who does what is wondrous for nature to accomplish in any manner — such as the pillar of cloud and the pillar of fire."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:41.387567231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}